## Credit

The idea of generating a UI mask from what holds still, and the "store the
masked pixels first, restore them last" arrangement this shader uses, come from
the UIDetectMulti shader pack by Kaiser, which in turn builds on work by
Brussels1. That project is licensed CC BY 4.0 and lives at
https://github.com/Kaiser-R/Reshade-Shaders

This shader shares no code with it: it was written from scratch, has no
companion configuration header, and needs no pixel coordinates or mask images.
The two are alternatives rather than companions, since both have to be first
and last in the effect list.

ReShade and its own header files (`ReShade.fxh`, `ReShadeUI.fxh`, `DrawText.fxh`)
belong to the ReShade project and are deliberately not vendored here.
